{"schemaVersion":1,"key":"fundamentals/tools","track":"everyone","lang":"en","dir":"ltr","title":"Tool Calling","words":1384,"objectives":{"lang":"en","items":["Explain why the AI never runs a tool itself, and who does","Name the four messages of one tool call, and who writes each one","Say why a tool's name and description decide whether the AI uses it well"]},"translatedObjectives":null,"prerequisites":[{"key":"fundamentals/llms","number":1,"title":"LLM Fundamentals","drawn":true,"track":"everyone","lang":"en"}],"previous":{"key":"fundamentals/rag","number":3,"title":"RAG & Embeddings","drawn":true,"track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"next":{"key":"fundamentals/memory","number":5,"title":"Memory","drawn":true,"track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"toc":[{"id":"why-this-matters-to-you","text":"Why This Matters to You","depth":2},{"id":"what-is-a-tool","text":"What is a Tool?","depth":2},{"id":"tool-calls-grow-context","text":"Tool Calls Grow Context","depth":2},{"id":"why-tools-exist","text":"Why Tools Exist","depth":2},{"id":"tool-schema","text":"Tool Schema","depth":2},{"id":"tool-call-in-action","text":"Tool Call in Action","depth":2},{"id":"example-tools","text":"Example Tools","depth":2},{"id":"words-you-now-know","text":"Words You Now Know","depth":2},{"id":"summary","text":"Summary","depth":2},{"id":"references","text":"References","depth":2},{"id":"-articles","text":"📄 Articles","depth":3}],"body":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"fundamentals/llms","track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"LLM Fundamentals"}]},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"fundamentals/training","track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Training LLMs"}]},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"fundamentals/rag","track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"RAG & Embeddings"}]},{"type":"text","text":" covered what a model is, how it learned, and how to put your own documents in front of it. In all of that, the AI only reads and writes. In this module, it starts "},{"type":"emphasis","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"doing"}]},{"type":"text","text":" things: it searches the web, reads a file, creates a calendar event or sends an email."}],"lead":true},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"This is the mechanism under every AI agent, so it is worth understanding exactly."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"why-this-matters-to-you","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Why This Matters to You"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"This is the step that turns a chatbot into an assistant that works for you. When an AI product says it can \"connect to your calendar\" or \"update your CRM\", it is using tools. Knowing how tools work tells you what such an assistant can really do, and what it could do by mistake."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-is-a-tool","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"What is a Tool?"}]},{"type":"image","number":"4.1","title":"An LLM reaching out through tools","note":"Tools are how a model reaches outside its own head. It searches the web, does maths or runs code, and then comes back with an answer.","src":"course-images/fundamentals/tools.webp","alt":"An LLM reaching out through tools","width":440,"height":242},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"tool"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is a small program that someone wrote. It has a name, a short description, and some details it needs, such as a city name or an email address."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is the part people get wrong: "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"the AI never runs the tool itself."}]},{"type":"text","text":" It cannot. It has no computer and no hands. The only thing it can do is write text."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"So go back to the chat picture from "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"fundamentals/llms","track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"LLM Fundamentals"}]},{"type":"text","text":". You ask \"what is the weather in Istanbul?\". The AI cannot know that. So instead of answering, it writes a special message: \"I would like to run "},{"type":"emphasis","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"check weather"}]},{"type":"text","text":" with city = Istanbul\". A normal program on a computer reads that message, runs the weather tool, and adds the result to the chat: \"34°C\". Then the AI reads the result and answers you. "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The AI asks; the computer does the work."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"tool-calls-grow-context","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Tool Calls Grow Context"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"A tool call adds two new kinds of message to the chat. This picture shows the whole flow:"}]},{"type":"image","number":"4.2","title":"The context of a single tool call","note":"One tool call, in order. The system prompt lists the tool before anyone speaks. Then you ask, and the AI writes a Tool Call. The computer runs it and writes the Tool Result. Then the AI reads that result and writes the answer.","src":"course-images/fundamentals/context-tool-call.webp","alt":"The context of a single tool call","width":1600,"height":893},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Follow the four arrows, because it matters who writes each message:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"You"}]},{"type":"text","text":" write your question."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The AI"}]},{"type":"text","text":" writes the "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"tool call"}]},{"type":"text","text":". It is asking, not doing."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The computer"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (your laptop, or a company server) runs the tool and writes the "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"tool result"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The AI"}]},{"type":"text","text":" reads the whole chat, which now includes that result, and writes the answer."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Both new messages stay in the chat. That is why an assistant's chat grows much faster than a normal chat: one question can add four or more messages instead of two."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"why-tools-exist","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Why Tools Exist"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"A model learned from data that stops at some date. So, on its own, it cannot know anything new, and it cannot change anything in the world. Tools fix both problems."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"It cannot search the web."}]},{"type":"text","text":" So someone writes a tool that searches the web and returns the results. Now it can."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"It cannot read your files."}]},{"type":"text","text":" So someone writes a tool that opens a file and returns what is inside. Now it can see your documents."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Without tools, an AI is a chatbot. With tools, it is an agent."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"tool-schema","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Tool Schema"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Before the AI can choose a tool, it has to know three things: that the tool exists, what it does, and what details it needs. That description is called the "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"tool schema"}]},{"type":"text","text":". Think of it as a menu card for the tool. It sits in the system prompt, at the top of the chat."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"A programmer writes the tool as a short piece of code, and software makes the menu card from it automatically. For example:"}]},{"type":"code","language":"python","lines":[[{"text":"@tool","role":"function"}],[{"text":"def","role":"keyword","bold":true},{"text":" get_weather","role":"function"},{"text":"(city: str) -> str:"}],[{"text":"    \"\"\"Get the current temperature for a city.\"\"\"","role":"string"}],[{"text":"    return","role":"keyword","bold":true},{"text":" requests."},{"text":"get(","role":"function"},{"text":"f","role":"keyword","bold":true},{"text":"\"https://api.example.com/weather?city=","role":"string"},{"text":"{","role":"number"},{"text":"city","role":"function"},{"text":"}","role":"number"},{"text":"\"","role":"string"},{"text":")","role":"function"},{"text":".text"}]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"If you do not read code, that is fine. Only three parts matter: the name ("},{"type":"code","text":"get_weather"},{"type":"text","text":"), the description in quotes, and the detail it needs ("},{"type":"code","text":"city"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is the key lesson: the AI chooses tools only from their menu cards."}]},{"type":"text","text":" The name and the description are the only things it sees. Imagine a tool called \"get data\", with the description \"gets data\". The AI will pick it at the wrong moments and skip it at the right ones. A clear name and a clear description are not decoration. They decide whether the assistant works well."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"tool-call-in-action","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Tool Call in Action"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is the weather example as it really happens:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The AI receives"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the system prompt with the weather tool's menu card, and your question: \"What is the weather in Istanbul?\""}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The AI writes a tool call"}]},{"type":"text","text":", not an answer. It looks something like this:"}]}]}]},{"type":"code","language":"json","lines":[[{"text":"{"}],[{"text":"  \"role\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"assistant\"","role":"string"},{"text":","}],[{"text":"  \"content\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"null","role":"number"},{"text":","}],[{"text":"  \"tool_calls\"","role":"string"},{"text":": ["}],[{"text":"    {"}],[{"text":"      \"id\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"call_9k2m4Xq7\"","role":"string"},{"text":","}],[{"text":"      \"type\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"function\"","role":"string"},{"text":","}],[{"text":"      \"function\"","role":"string"},{"text":": {"}],[{"text":"        \"name\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"get_weather\"","role":"string"},{"text":","}],[{"text":"        \"arguments\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"{","role":"string"},{"text":"\\\"","role":"number"},{"text":"city","role":"string"},{"text":"\\\"","role":"number"},{"text":":","role":"string"},{"text":"\\\"","role":"number"},{"text":"Istanbul","role":"string"},{"text":"\\\"","role":"number"},{"text":"}\"","role":"string"}],[{"text":"      }"}],[{"text":"    }"}],[{"text":"  ]"}],[{"text":"}"}]]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The computer"}]},{"type":"text","text":" sees the request, runs the weather tool with \"Istanbul\", and adds the result to the chat: "},{"type":"code","text":"34°C, sunny"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The AI reads everything again"}]},{"type":"text","text":", including the result, and writes: \"It is 34°C and sunny in Istanbul.\""}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Every AI agent you will ever use repeats these same steps, again and again."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Some chat screens show these steps as they happen. In this recording, each stock lookup appears as a card, so you can see what the AI asked for and what came back."}]},{"type":"image","number":"4.3","title":"Tool calls shown as cards","note":"Each card is one tool use: what the AI asked for (a stock) and what the tool answered. There is one card for each stock. Recorded from a demo in CopilotKit's AG-UI Dojo.","src":"course-images/fundamentals/tool-call-cards.webp","alt":"Tool calls shown as cards","width":990,"height":794},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example-tools","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Example Tools"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Almost anything a computer can do can become a tool:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"search the web"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"read or search company documents (this is the RAG search from "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"fundamentals/rag","track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"RAG & Embeddings"}]},{"type":"text","text":", turned into a tool, so the AI decides "},{"type":"emphasis","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"when"}]},{"type":"text","text":" to look something up)"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"send an email from Gmail"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"create a ticket in Jira"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"add an event to your calendar"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"look up a number in a database"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Most useful tools are a thin wrapper around a service your company already uses."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Gmail, your calendar and your payment system already have a way for programs to talk to them. The tool only connects the AI to that."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Two warnings come with this. First, "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"a tool is exactly as powerful as the access you give it."}]},{"type":"text","text":" A tool that can send email from your account can send anything to anyone. For HR and finance work, think carefully before you give an assistant that kind of access. Second, you rarely have to build these tools yourself any more. A standard called "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"MCP"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (Model Context Protocol) packages tools so that one tool works in any AI assistant. Often someone has already built the one you need. The "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"intermediate/coding-agents","track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Code Agents"}]},{"type":"text","text":" module covers it."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"words-you-now-know","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Words You Now Know"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Tool"}]},{"type":"text","text":": a small program the AI can ask to run, such as \"check weather\" or \"send email\"."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Tool call"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the AI's message asking for a tool to run."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Tool result"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the answer the computer adds to the chat after running the tool."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Tool schema"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the tool's menu card: its name, description and the details it needs."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Host"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the computer that actually runs the tool."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"MCP"}]},{"type":"text","text":": a standard way to package tools so any AI assistant can use them."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"summary","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Summary"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The AI cannot do anything except write text. So when it needs something from the world, it writes a tool call, a normal program runs the tool, and the result goes back into the chat. The AI chooses tools only from their menu cards, so a clear name and description matter. And a tool can do whatever its access allows, so access is a decision to take seriously."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Next comes memory: what an AI remembers, and where."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Quick check"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Who runs the tool, the AI or the computer? What are the four steps of one tool call, and who does each? And why does a vague tool name make an assistant worse?"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"references","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"References"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"-articles","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"📄 Articles"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://machinelearningmastery.com/mastering-llm-tool-calling-the-complete-framework-for-connecting-models-to-the-real-world/"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Mastering LLM tool calling"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the full picture, with more technical detail"}]}]}]}],"draft":null,"quiz":[{"question":"A model decides to call the tool `read_file`. Who runs the function?","options":["The model runs the function inside its own weights.","The framework sends the function to the model, and the model runs it.","The host machine runs the function and writes the Tool Result.","The user runs the function and types the result into the chat."],"answer":2,"explain":"The model has no computer, so it only writes a Tool Call that asks for the function. The host machine, your laptop or your server, runs it and writes the Tool Result."},{"question":"Why does an agent's context grow faster than a chat's context?","options":["Each Tool Call and each Tool Result stay in the context.","Each tool call adds a new system prompt to the context.","The model must write a longer answer after each tool call.","The user must ask the question again after each tool call."],"answer":0,"explain":"A tool call adds two new messages: the Tool Call and the Tool Result. Both stay in the context, so one turn can add several messages instead of two."},{"question":"You write a function with the `@tool` decorator. Where does the framework get the tool's description?","options":["From the function name, `get_weather`.","From the type hints, for example `city: str`.","From a JSON file that you write by hand.","From the docstring of the function."],"answer":3,"explain":"The framework generates the tool schema for you, and it reads the description from the docstring. The name comes from the function name, and the parameters come from the type hints."},{"question":"Your tool is called `get_data` and its docstring says \"gets data\". The model picks it at the wrong moments. What fixes this?","options":["Add more instructions about the tool to the system prompt.","Rename the tool and rewrite its docstring for the model.","Make the code inside the function faster and more correct.","Add longer comments inside the body of the function."],"answer":1,"explain":"The name and the description are the only things the model uses to choose a tool. More prompting does not fix a vague name and docstring."},{"question":"In the Tool Call message, the model writes an `id`, for example `call_9k2m4Xq7`. What is it for?","options":["It tells the host machine which Python file to open.","It counts how many tools the model called in this chat.","It matches the Tool Result back to this specific call.","It identifies the user who asked the question."],"answer":2,"explain":"The host machine tags the Tool Result with the same `id`, in the field `tool_call_id`. This links the result to the call that asked for it."}]}